{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/963","id":4462770330,"node_id":"PR_kwDOH8_sKs8AAAABCgB4mg","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/963","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/963.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/963.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/963","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/963/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/963/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/963/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/statuses/8a2106aaf4256a8883d7b61aaaae119729b6530e","number":963,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Reach 100% test coverage","user":{"login":"hramezani","id":3122442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjI0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3122442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani","html_url":"https://github.com/hramezani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nBrings `pydantic_settings` to **100% statement and branch coverage** (from ~99%) by adding tests for genuinely uncovered behavior and marking the unreachable defensive branches with `pragma`.\n\n## The reason it wasn't already 100%\n\nThe ~99% figure is measured on a **single interpreter**. CI already combines coverage across `{ubuntu, macos, windows} × py{3.10–3.14}` plus a \"test without deps\" run, and several \"uncovered\" lines were never test gaps — they are version- or platform-gated code that only executes on another matrix leg:\n\n| Lines | Only runs on |\n|---|---|\n| `toml.py:36-39,77` vs `43-45,78` | py<3.11 vs py≥3.11 |\n| `types.py:11` vs `13` | py≥3.11 vs py<3.11 |\n| `yaml.py:32-33` | the PyYAML-uninstalled run |\n\nVerified empirically: on 3.10 the report shows the *opposite* toml/types lines missing, and combining py3.10 + py3.12 + a no-PyYAML run drops misses to zero.\n\n```\nName    Stmts   Miss Branch BrPart    Cover\n-----------------------------------------------------\nTOTAL    2581      0   1088      0  100.00%\n```\n\nA single `make test` will still report ~99% — that is expected, and no Makefile target was added for the combine since it wasn't in scope.\n\n## New tests\n\n- **AWS Secrets Manager** — `version_id` pinning reads a pinned version rather than latest\n- **Azure Key Vault** — case-sensitive/insensitive secret mapping, `__len__`, `__repr__`\n- **GCP Secret Manager** — project-resolution caching, unknown versioned aliases\n- **CLI** — unknown-arg rejection with a non-argparse root parser, nested-alias env var prefixing, duplicate env var name de-duplication, model description fallbacks\n- **CliApp** — async `cli_cmd` exception propagation out of the worker thread\n- **Env** — `Json` and strict value coercion paths\n- **YAML** — nested-section traversal fallbacks\n- Assorted helpers in `sources/utils.py` and `sources/base.py`\n\nThe Windows case-insensitivity fallback from #295 was previously exercised only by the Windows CI leg. It now also has a test that patches the probe, so it runs on every platform — the existing Windows-skipped test still covers the real integration.\n\n## Non-test changes\n\n- **8 `pragma` markers** on code traced to be genuinely unreachable, each with a comment explaining why. For example, `main.py`'s init-kwarg fallback (`InitSettingsSource` always normalizes to the preferred alias, so that alias is always present in state) and `gcp.py`'s lowercase retry (`_extract_field_info` already lower-cases when case-insensitive).\n- **One structural tweak**: `main.py`'s alias-selection loop became a `next(...)` expression. Identical behavior, but it stops reporting a partial branch that no input could take.\n\nNo behavior changes.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `784 passed, 6 skipped` on py3.12; `783 passed, 7 skipped` on py3.10\n- [x] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` clean\n- [x] `mypy` reports the same 14 pre-existing errors as `main` (missing optional stubs locally) — confirmed via `git stash`\n- [x] Combined coverage across py3.10 + py3.12 + no-deps run = 100.00%\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01F7HypPgSUD8cVkNETX12Sk","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-07T10:00:13Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T11:05:22Z","closed_at":"2026-09-07T11:05:20Z","merged_at":"2026-09-07T11:05:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"d357d7bf3183d4c658afa266acb4c3c7cdd6be0e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"pydantic:improve-test-coverage","ref":"improve-test-coverage","repo":{"id":533720106,"node_id":"R_kgDOH8_sKg","name":"pydantic-settings","full_name":"pydantic/pydantic-settings","owner":{"login":"pydantic","id":110818415,"node_id":"O_kgDOBpr0bw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/110818415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pydantic","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/us